  <p>Denver is the second launch metro because official operator pages treat it as a high-demand gateway: Native Campervans’ Denver page says the company started there in 2015, and Cruise America’s Denver page says rental demand spikes around major events and recommends booking early. Those are first-party statements, not a claim that every weekend is sold out. Los Angeles is the other launch market because national fleets and several local campervan depots publish addresses across the metro.</p>
  <p>Those pages are verified samples, not a complete inventory of either city. We do not cache live unit prices or available rigs. If a listing includes a price, it is labeled as listed on a date.</p>

